Here's a clean, flexible implementation that retries a callback up to N times if it throws an error:

```javascript
/**
 * Retries a callback up to `maxRetries` times if it throws an error.
 *
 * @param {Function} fn - The callback to execute (can be async or sync)
 * @param {number} maxRetries - Maximum number of retry attempts
 * @param {Object} [options] - Optional configuration
 * @param {number} [options.delay=0] - Delay in ms between retries
 * @param {Function} [options.onRetry] - Called before each retry with (error, attempt)
 * @returns {Promise<*>} - Resolves with the callback's return value
 */
async function retry(fn, maxRetries, options = {}) {
  const { delay = 0, onRetry } = options;

  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= maxRetries + 1; attempt++) {
